{"abstract":"Most users interact with explainable AI (XAI) systems through an interface. Despite the growing assemblage of human-centered XAI literature, there is still limited research that investigates how explanations are presented in interfaces. With this preliminary study, we propose a novel approach to analyze the content and interactions of explainable interfaces by mapping UI elements and interactions to the type of explanation they convey. Based on analysis of 28 explainable interfaces, we offer initial findings of how various interaction concepts and UI elements are used to provide different explanations.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Meyer, Louie Søs","Zhu, Jichen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776455"],"event":{"end":"2024-10-16","place":"Uppsala, se","start":"2024-10-13","title":"Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Explanation types","Human centered XAI"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"slide to explore what if an analysis of explainable interfaces","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-776455","identifier":[{"id":"85206566341","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e8c86569-6691-40c8-8ebd-b350b2457a54"],"keyword":["explainable AI interfaces","explanation types","human-centered XAI","interaction concepts","user interface elements"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-4B609534EF776E26E913CA7B77026F59"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Human-AI Interaction Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louie Søs","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"b55a7155-5e64-4230-b7da-94f7872e9742","name":"Meyer, Louie Søs","orcid":"0009-0008-7490-3049","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jichen","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","locid":"e383647f-00d3-41b1-ad95-ff69bdfffb42","name":"Zhu, Jichen","orcid":"0000-0001-6740-4550","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3677045.3685416","journal":"Proceedings of NordiCHI","pages":"1-6","paperid":"2","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of NordiCHI"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85206566341"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e8c86569-6691-40c8-8ebd-b350b2457a54"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Slide to Explore 'What If': An Analysis of Explainable Interfaces","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776455","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This Research through Design paper explores how object detection may be applied to a large digital art museum collection to facilitate new ways of encountering and experiencing art. We present the design and evaluation of an interactive application called SMKExplore, which allows users to explore a museum’s digital collection of paintings by browsing through objects detected in the images, as a novel form of open-ended exploration. We provide three contributions. First, we show how an object detection pipeline can be integrated into a design process for visual exploration. Second, we present the design and development of an app that enables exploration of an art museum’s collection. Third, we offer reflections on future possibilities for museums and HCI researchers to incorporate object detection techniques into the digitalization of museums.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Meyer, Louie Søs","Engel Aaen, Johanne","Tranberg, Anitamalina Regitse","Kun, Peter","Freiberger, Matthias","Risi, Sebastian","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776388"],"event":{"end":"2024-05-16","place":"Honolulu, us","start":"2024-05-11","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Art","Computer vision","Experience Design","Exploratory search","Object detection"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"algorithmic ways of seeing using object detection to facilitate art exploration","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3613904.3642157","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776388","identifier":[{"id":"8